745","name":"Simon","also":"Cephas, Simeon","summary":"Originally called Simon (=Simeon, i.e., “hearing”), a very common Jewish name in the New Testament. He was the son of Jona (Matt. 16:17). His mother is nowhere named in Scripture.","verses":175,"father":"Jonas","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"james_719","name":"James","also":"","summary":"The son of Alphaeus, or Cleopas, “the brother” or near kinsman or cousin of our Lord (Gal. 1:18, 19), called James “the Less,” or “the Little,” probably because he was of low stature.","verses":15,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Mary","v":[19]}],"places":[{"id":"galatia_431","name":"Galatia","kind":"Region","lat":37.5,"lon":32.5,"summary":"Has been called the “Gallia” of the East, Roman writers calling its inhabitants Galli. They were an intermixture of Gauls and Greeks, and hence were called Gallo-Graeci, and the country Gallo-Graecia.","verses":6,"v":[2]},{"id":"arabia_80","name":"Arabia","kind":"Region","lat":27.4,"lon":37.7,"summary":"Arabia Petraea, i.e., the Rocky Arabia, so called from its rocky mountains and stony plains. It comprehended all the north-west portion of the country, and is much better known to travellers than any other portion.","verses":6,"v":[17]},{"id":"damascus_322","name":"Damascus","kind":"City","lat":33.51161,"lon":36.3091,"summary":"Activity, the most ancient of Oriental cities; the capital of Syria (Isa. 7:8; 17:3); situated about 133 miles to the north of Jerusalem.","verses":55,"v":[17]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[17,18]},{"id":"cilicia_300","name":"Cilicia","kind":"Region","lat":36.91803,"lon":34.89153,"summary":"A maritime province in the south-east of Asia Minor. Tarsus, the birth-place of Paul, was one of its chief towns, and the seat of a celebrated school of philosophy.","verses":8,"v":[21]},{"id":"syria_1122","name":"Syria","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":37.5,"lon":37.5,"summary":"(Heb. Aram), the name in the Old Testament given to the whole country which lay to the north-east of Phoenicia, extending to beyond the Euphrates and the Tigris.","verses":64,"v":[21]},{"id":"judea_657","name":"Judea","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"After the Captivity this name was applied to the whole of the country west of the Jordan (Hag. 1:1, 14; 2:2).","verses":44,"v":[22]}],"events":[{"id":"paul_writes_galatians_347","title":"Paul Writes Galatians","year":49,"summary":"Passage: Galatians 1:1. People: Paul.","v":[1]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3972,652,652,3756,575,444,3761,1223,444,235,1223,2424,5547,2532,2316,3962,3962,3588,1453,846,1537,3498,3498],[2532,3956,3588,80,4862,1473,3588,3588,1577,1053,1053],[5485,2532,1515,4771,4771,575,2316,1473,3962,2532,2962,2962,2424,5547],[3588,1325,1438,5228,1473,266,3704,1807,1473,1537,3588,1764,4190,165,2596,2596,3588,2307,1473,1473,2316,2532,3962],[3739,3739,3739,1391,165,3588,165,281],[2296,2296,2296,3779,5030,3346,3346,3346,3588,3588,3588,2564,4771,1722,5485,5485,5547,5547,1519,1519,1519,1519,2087,2087,2098],[3739,1510,3756,3756,243,243,1487,5100,3588,1510,5015,4771,2532,2309,3344,3344,3588,2098,5547,5547],[235,2532,1437,1473,2228,32,32,1537,3772,2097,2097,2097,2097,3844,3844,3739,3739,2097,2097,4771,4771,1510,1510,1510,331,331,331],[5613,4302,4302,4302,4302,2532,737,3004,3004,3825,1487,5100,2097,2097,2097,2097,2097,2097,3844,3844,3739,3739,3880,3880,1510,1510,1510,331,331,331],[737,737,737,3982,3982,3982,444,444,2228,2316,2316,2228,2212,2212,2212,700,700,444,1487,700,700,700,700,700,700,444,1510,1510,1510,1510,1401,1401,5547,5547],[1063,1107,1107,1107,1107,1107,80,3588,3588,2098,2097,2097,1510,3756,2596,2596,444],[1473,3761,3761,3880,846,3844,444,444,3777,1321,1321,1321,1321,235,235,235,235,1223,602,2424,2424,5547]